WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.520
You're dreaming big and doing absolutely

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:07.440
nothing about it. You've had this same

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:10.200
idea for 2 years, maybe 3 years, a great

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:13.000
dream for your career, your business,

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:15.560
your relationships, wealth maybe, but

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.520
you haven't started yet. Why? What's

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:20.120
getting in the way? That's what we want

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:22.920
to cover. There's three traps. I've had

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:25.520
this dream for over 5 years. Never got

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:28.080
started on it until last year. And it

00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:31.360
was [music] to start this very YouTube

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:34.680
channel. And when I finally did it,

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:37.080
all I could think of was, "Man, I should

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:40.320
have done it much sooner." In the last 8

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:43.040
months, we've added 1.2 [music] million

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.720
subscribers. For every second that this

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:48.440
channel has been alive, roughly about 45

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:50.960
million seconds, someone somewhere has

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:54.840
watched [music] a video. The love and

00:00:50.960 --> 00:00:56.960
the warmth that I continue to receive

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.440
every [music] day is just

00:00:56.960 --> 00:01:02.225
overwhelming. It's so hard to describe.

00:00:59.440 --> 00:01:04.120
Just impossible. So, that's the story

00:01:02.225 --> 00:01:06.320
[music] I want to share today. That's

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:08.320
our case study. And through that, we

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:11.480
will build a systematic process [music]

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:13.920
that helps you define those three traps

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:15.880
and gets you out of all three of them.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.400
The third one took me 20 [music] years

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:20.680
to figure out.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:24.320
And this video I thought would be

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:26.400
different. It's raw. It's no animations,

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:28.200
no effects, just unplugged. Because

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.520
we're talking about the YouTube channel

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.520
itself, I thought it should be just you

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:33.360
and me.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:36.160
And I have the cameras on and I have

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:37.960
some bullet points in front of me, but

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:39.720
it's just going to be a conversation.

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:43.320
So, let's get going. I think the first

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.240
trap is the hardest to escape, at least

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:48.800
for me.

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:51.080
We don't bet on ourselves. Our ambition

00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:54.800
is not a problem. I think the real

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:57.960
problem is how we see ourselves. I'm not

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.520
worthy. I don't deserve it, who's going

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:03.000
to care?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:05.000
You would rather take a chance on anyone

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:08.600
but yourself.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:11.240
That's been my story all my life.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:14.760
In fact, the genesis of this very

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:17.959
channel will tell you all about how that

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:21.720
narrative has been trapping all of us. I

00:02:17.959 --> 00:02:24.120
was a young kid, a teenager, and I ran

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:26.120
away from home for a while, and I became

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.520
a monk in training,

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:29.959
swept the courtyards and cleaned the

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:33.920
toilets and

00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:36.480
ate one meal a day from a bowl, all of

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:37.959
that. And and somehow,

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.760
over time,

00:02:37.959 --> 00:02:44.720
I managed to become a musician and ended

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:47.160
up going to MIT, worked on Wall Street,

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.520
eventually became a CEO, board member,

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:51.400
investor, all of that. But all

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:54.880
throughout that journey,

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:57.520
at every phase, the voice that has

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:59.280
always kept repeating in my head has

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:01.239
been saying,

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:04.360
"What am I doing here? I don't belong

00:03:01.239 --> 00:03:07.000
here. I'm not supposed to be here." And

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:10.239
eventually, I got very lucky,

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:13.320
and I had two big exits, and I was in

00:03:10.239 --> 00:03:16.360
tech, so I got to retire about 3 years

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:18.760
ago. But even after that, this idea that

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:20.440
I don't deserve it has

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:22.760
never left me.

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:25.239
I don't know, it must be my chemistry or

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:28.200
something. When I thought, "Oh, I should

00:03:25.239 --> 00:03:30.760
start something creative. I should start

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:34.680
a YouTube channel." Because I saw my

00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:37.000
8-year-old being completely fearless

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:40.519
in starting his channel.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:43.040
And I thought, "Well, if he could do it,

00:03:40.519 --> 00:03:44.640
I can do it, too." But I was still so

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:48.040
afraid

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:51.480
about going it alone. So, I went back to

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:53.120
my old band members. Uh one by one, I

00:03:51.480 --> 00:03:56.160
asked all of them

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:58.080
to see if they would do it with me.

00:03:56.160 --> 00:03:59.720
If we could start the band together and

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:02.800
then the YouTube channel would be about

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:03.840
music. And in that band I was the

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:07.320
drummer.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:10.840
So, I was never used to being in the

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:12.160
center. You know, I was only comfortable

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:15.600
on

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:17.239
being on the side or at the back. And

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.880
unfortunately, they were all busy with

00:04:17.239 --> 00:04:22.160
their own lives and their own dreams.

00:04:18.880 --> 00:04:26.040
So, nothing came of it. And I remember

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:28.760
feeling so down about it. And one late

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:29.880
evening, I was flying from London to New

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.800
York.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:35.880
And this

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:38.680
thought suddenly hit me that I was just

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:40.320
hiding behind them.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:43.840
I've been doing that all my life. I

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:47.960
always wanted a partner, a co-founder.

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:50.800
I had never bet on myself. And that's

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:53.600
where I decided to just

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.680
talk about personal growth, professional

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:58.760
growth,

00:04:54.680 --> 00:05:02.400
AI, careers, finance, relationships,

00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:03.600
insights that the 22-year-old version of

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:07.280
me

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:11.000
needed so desperately but never got. So,

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:14.560
that's how this channel came about. So,

00:05:11.000 --> 00:05:18.320
I went ahead and I hired an agency, a

00:05:14.560 --> 00:05:20.919
team uh, to help me edit and manage this

00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:24.440
whole YouTube channel and the process.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:27.120
And I remember them asking me, "Hey,

00:05:24.440 --> 00:05:30.680
what do you want to call it?"

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:32.320
And I said, "Listen, you can call it

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:35.400
whatever you want

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:40.200
as long as it's not my own name."

00:05:35.400 --> 00:05:42.560
Still hiding. So, we found a brand name.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:45.520
Some of you may remember that this

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:49.240
channel's original name was The MIT

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:52.720
Monk. And I love that name.

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:54.000
Two contrasting ideas and I had been

00:05:52.720 --> 00:05:55.560
both.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.240
However,

00:05:55.560 --> 00:06:00.200
I remember

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:02.640
heaving a sigh of relief when we found

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:04.960
the name. And the first thought that

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.480
came to my mind was

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:09.480
great.

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:12.320
This is all about this thing called MIT

00:06:09.480 --> 00:06:14.480
Monk, this avatar.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:18.320
I don't have to be

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:22.560
me. I don't have to bet on myself. So,

00:06:18.320 --> 00:06:26.120
anyway, the first video gets released in

00:06:22.560 --> 00:06:28.960
February of 2025, the long-form video.

00:06:26.120 --> 00:06:33.720
For the first 8 months after that,

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:35.480
uh so, until October, November of 2025,

00:06:33.720 --> 00:06:37.800
crickets.

00:06:35.480 --> 00:06:39.760
Very few people watched

00:06:37.800 --> 00:06:42.800
what I was producing,

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:44.680
even fewer subscribers. And you know,

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:47.520
I was kind of relieved.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:51.200
I wasn't surprised, either, because, you

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:54.560
know, there are 140 million videos

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:57.720
uploaded on YouTube every week. And, you

00:06:54.560 --> 00:07:00.400
know, my mine was one of them.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:03.080
Lost in the same void. Fortunately, I

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:06.240
did not need to make money off of this

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:08.360
channel. So, I kept showing up every

00:07:06.240 --> 00:07:11.680
week, week after week.

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:17.120
And I remember we crossed about 50,000

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:22.200
subscribers in late October of 2025. And

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:25.600
I still heard the same voice. Why will

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:28.800
anyone care what I have to say? So, I

00:07:25.600 --> 00:07:33.560
remember I was on a Zoom call with the

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:37.600
agency CEO and the creative director.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:42.360
And I asked them, you know, it's October

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:45.960
and we're at 50,000 subscribers or so.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:49.360
When do you think we'll cross

00:07:45.960 --> 00:07:51.960
100,000 subscribers?" And

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:55.120
they looked at each other and said, "You

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:56.800
know, at this rate, it will take you

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:58.360
at least a year

00:07:56.800 --> 00:07:59.640
or more."

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:03.960
So,

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:07.040
October of 2026, maybe. And that's when

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:10.160
we will cross 100,000 subscribers.

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:14.480
And I was delighted. I was happy

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:17.880
with that expert forecast.

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:20.080
But then, something surprising started

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:22.120
happening in November. And I remember,

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:25.880
it was like November 1st or something

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:25.880
like that. Just water break.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:31.240
Because we crossed

00:08:28.919 --> 00:08:33.520
100,000 subscribers

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:35.520
in literally 2 weeks

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:37.840
after that Zoom call. Whatever was

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:40.599
supposed to take a year, we crossed it

00:08:37.840 --> 00:08:41.800
in 2 weeks. And in 8 months since

00:08:40.599 --> 00:08:44.839
November,

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:47.839
we added 1.2 million subscribers.

00:08:44.839 --> 00:08:51.400
And the growth keeps accelerating.

00:08:47.839 --> 00:08:52.880
I kid you not. I don't really know why

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:55.920
that happened.

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:59.640
I don't really know why it's happening.

00:08:55.920 --> 00:09:02.520
I have some theories about it, but

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:06.280
YouTube algorithm is an algorithm of

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:07.600
attention. So, why do millions of

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:10.720
people,

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:14.640
viewers like you, decide to give their

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:16.640
time and their attention and their love

00:09:14.640 --> 00:09:20.680
to someone like me

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:25.600
is a a total mystery box that I can't

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:28.320
solve. All I can do is feel this immense

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:31.080
gratitude that

00:09:28.320 --> 00:09:33.839
we get to spend time together and this

00:09:31.080 --> 00:09:35.960
thing keeps growing

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:38.800
every day. But then,

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:40.880
uh came one more twist.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:43.440
As we were crossing that million

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:48.851
subscriber milestone in

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:49.200
April or May of of uh, 2026, MIT called.

00:09:48.851 --> 00:09:51.520
>> [laughter]

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:53.360
>> And they they were

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:54.560
like very nice, you know, they were

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:58.640
gentle.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:10:00.400
And they said, "Hey, you know,

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:02.920
we love the fact that you were doing

00:10:00.400 --> 00:10:05.640
this. It's it's uh, very nice. The

00:10:02.920 --> 00:10:09.440
content is very good. But we're going to

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:11.400
have to ask you to take down MIT from

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:13.280
the brand name that you're using because

00:10:11.400 --> 00:10:15.800
people

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:18.840
thought that there was an actual monk

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:19.840
that worked at MIT as a faculty member.

00:10:18.840 --> 00:10:22.720
So,

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:25.680
of course, we I said yes because I am an

00:10:22.720 --> 00:10:28.160
alum. My team started scrambling for

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:29.720
another brand name. I have this chief of

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.800
staff of mine and I've worked with her

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:35.520
for years. She's known me for years.

00:10:32.800 --> 00:10:36.480
And she asked me to get on a live Zoom

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:37.920
call.

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:41.160
And she

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:45.360
literally shared her desktop screen on

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:47.480
Zoom and looked me in the eye and said,

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:50.480
"I'm going to change the name right

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:53.480
now." And before I could say anything,

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:56.120
she added my real name

00:10:53.480 --> 00:11:00.839
on the YouTube channel homepage.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:11:03.400
The MIT Monk became Sandeep Sodhiya. And

00:11:00.839 --> 00:11:05.480
it felt so uncomfortable

00:11:03.400 --> 00:11:08.440
for me to see that name.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:10.760
I just wanted to keep hiding. Now,

00:11:08.440 --> 00:11:12.440
I've been to the absolute bottom and

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:16.040
I've been to the top. I've been very

00:11:12.440 --> 00:11:18.839
fortunate. I'm not scared of losing.

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:20.080
But standing up in the spotlight all by

00:11:18.839 --> 00:11:23.400
yourself

00:11:20.080 --> 00:11:25.160
and then accepting that you can deserve

00:11:23.400 --> 00:11:28.160
to be there,

00:11:25.160 --> 00:11:31.240
that's super hard. And researchers have

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:34.680
looked at hundreds of studies on this.

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:36.440
Only about half the people who intend to

00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:38.560
do something

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:41.240
who intend to follow their dreams end up

00:11:38.560 --> 00:11:44.160
doing it. It's a coin flip. So, it's

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:48.440
never about how badly you want it.

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:52.080
Doing is way harder than dreaming.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:54.760
We get in our own way. So, what do you

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:57.480
do this Monday morning?

00:11:54.760 --> 00:12:00.600
First, you have to realize that

00:11:57.480 --> 00:12:02.840
you are waiting for your own permission

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:05.400
that will never come.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:08.160
And second, start with the smallest of

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:11.080
the small bet that you can make.

00:12:08.160 --> 00:12:13.320
Just the first step. Take it.

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:17.400
Because this is what you will tell me

00:12:13.320 --> 00:12:20.080
later. I guarantee it. You'll say

00:12:17.400 --> 00:12:22.080
I should have started it much sooner.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:25.560
It doesn't matter if

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:27.600
no one else cares. If you care about it

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:30.040
deeply,

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:33.480
isn't that a great reason enough to get

00:12:30.040 --> 00:12:37.520
started? And here's another example. I

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:39.920
love going deeper, and so I started

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:43.040
writing a newsletter I think 2 months

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:46.400
ago. Every Tuesday it comes out, and one

00:12:43.040 --> 00:12:48.880
insight, one tool, one practice

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:51.120
that you can use every day.

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:53.520
And and you can subscribe to it if you'd

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:57.000
like, but it's something I

00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:59.280
I love to do. That's a reason enough.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:13:01.160
It's free. Link is below.

00:12:59.280 --> 00:13:02.080
But let's talk about the second trap

00:13:01.160 --> 00:13:04.640
now.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:04.640
And that is

00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:09.800
subtle

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:11.880
and trickier.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:13.600
And I hear about it

00:13:11.880 --> 00:13:16.800
from

00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:21.120
thousands of inbound messages.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:22.920
The question is, why start anything in

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:25.120
the age of AI?

00:13:22.920 --> 00:13:27.400
The machines can do it better than me

00:13:25.120 --> 00:13:30.960
and faster than me.

00:13:27.400 --> 00:13:35.960
Some of it is partly true and it feels

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:35.960
like you lost before you even started.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:41.400
But, I think as AI gets smarter at

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:45.480
intelligence,

00:13:41.400 --> 00:13:48.200
our human judgment is going to be more

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:49.960
and more valuable. Let me give you two

00:13:48.200 --> 00:13:51.440
examples.

00:13:49.960 --> 00:13:54.560
Two stories.

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:57.520
One about creation and one about

00:13:54.560 --> 00:13:59.680
communication. Both stories are coming

00:13:57.520 --> 00:14:02.120
from building this YouTube channel

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:04.920
because that's our case study.

00:14:02.120 --> 00:14:08.160
But, the activity doesn't matter. The

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:11.120
principles will apply to anything you

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:14.240
want to build in the age of AI.

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:17.440
So, for every week,

00:14:14.240 --> 00:14:20.480
I think about what I what the topics are

00:14:17.440 --> 00:14:22.160
going to be, what I want to talk about,

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:25.160
and I write

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:27.640
the script every week. And, that's the

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:30.640
biggest challenge because there's so

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:33.440
much AI slop on YouTube, as you know, on

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:37.920
any social media platform nowadays. And,

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:40.360
building something original seems almost

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:43.800
impossible because

00:14:40.360 --> 00:14:46.640
AI, by default, wants you to talk like

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:49.320
everybody else. That's how AI learned to

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:51.960
talk anyway because it was trained on

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:55.000
the content that existed on the

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:56.800
internet. Creating something

00:14:55.000 --> 00:15:00.760
truly original

00:14:56.800 --> 00:15:04.839
takes two human faculties that aren't

00:15:00.760 --> 00:15:07.800
supposed to get along well. Your

00:15:04.839 --> 00:15:10.880
hot-blooded emotions and your

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:12.880
cold-blooded craft. They fight each

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:15.120
other all the time because when you

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:18.800
focus on your emotions and your

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:22.240
intuition and your imagination, you lose

00:15:18.800 --> 00:15:25.360
sight of the discipline to focus on the

00:15:22.240 --> 00:15:27.600
details of grammar and structure and and

00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:29.880
verification of the research and all of

00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:32.800
that stuff. And on the other hand, when

00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:34.760
you focus on the craft and the details

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:37.600
and the structures that you want to

00:15:34.760 --> 00:15:39.880
neatly construct something,

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:43.440
then you lose that spark, that that

00:15:39.880 --> 00:15:46.720
intuition, that that humanness of it.

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:48.840
There is a great Indian poet

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:51.880
and I love him. I admire his work. His

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:56.120
name is Javed Akhtar and he

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:58.000
says it brilliantly that it is this very

00:15:56.120 --> 00:16:00.920
contradiction

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:03.360
that makes our output human, that makes

00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:07.160
our output poetic.

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:08.560
It gives it the the unique fingerprint

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:10.840
that is yours.

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:13.680
Here's the thing, the cold half, you

00:16:10.840 --> 00:16:16.680
know, the craft and the structure and

00:16:13.680 --> 00:16:19.880
and ideation, all of that, a machine can

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:21.360
do that now instantly and free, and

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:23.600
better than you and faster than you.

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:25.360
What it cannot do

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:28.880
is the other half.

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:31.880
That's your imagination, your intuition,

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:34.320
your judgment. And

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:37.240
working through this contradiction of

00:16:34.320 --> 00:16:39.880
